## Correct solution

The original order matters: we cannot necessarily keep the largest elements.

Let
\[
m=\left\lfloor\frac{n-1}{k}\right\rfloor,\qquad r=n-mk.
\]
Exactly \(m\) operations are performed, leaving \(r\) elements.

### 1. Characterize possible remaining arrays

Suppose the surviving elements originally had indices
\[
p_1<p_2<\dots<p_r.
\]

Each gap before, between, or after survivors must contain a multiple of \(k\) deleted elements. This is necessary because a deletion cannot cross an element that survives. It is also sufficient: delete each gap in chunks of \(k\).

Consequently, valid indices have the form
\[
p_j=j+k b_j,\qquad
0\le b_1\le b_2\le\dots\le b_r\le m.
\]

### 2. Check whether a median of at least \(x\) is possible

Call an element good if it is at least \(x\).

For the lower median to be at least \(x\), the remaining array must contain at least
\[
\left\lfloor\frac r2\right\rfloor+1
\]
good elements.

Use dynamic programming over the possible values of \(b_j\).

Process \(b=0,1,\ldots,m\). Let `dp[j]` be the maximum number of good elements obtainable by choosing the first \(j\) survivors with their block numbers at most the current \(b\).

For each block, process \(j=1,\ldots,r\) in increasing order:
```text
dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[j-1] + (a[b*k+j-1] >= x))
```

The existing value skips this block for survivor \(j\). The second choice puts survivor \(j\) in this block. Increasing iteration order permits consecutive survivors to use the same block.

Binary-search the answer among the distinct array values.

### C++17 code

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

void solve() {
    int n, k;
    cin >> n >> k;

    vector<int> a(n);
    for (int &x : a) cin >> x;

    int m = (n - 1) / k;
    int r = n - m * k;
    int required = r / 2 + 1;

    auto possible = [&](int x) {
        vector<int> dp(r + 1, -n - 1);
        dp[0] = 0;

        for (int b = 0; b <= m; ++b) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= r; ++j) {
                int index = b * k + j - 1;
                dp[j] = max(dp[j],
                            dp[j - 1] + (a[index] >= x));
            }
        }

        return dp[r] >= required;
    };

    vector<int> values = a;
    sort(values.begin(), values.end());
    values.erase(unique(values.begin(), values.end()), values.end());

    int lo = 0, hi = (int)values.size() - 1;
    while (lo < hi) {
        int mid = lo + (hi - lo + 1) / 2;
        if (possible(values[mid])) {
            lo = mid;
        } else {
            hi = mid - 1;
        }
    }

    cout << values[lo] << '\n';
}

